Week 4
Week 4 (09/22–09/28)

This week I used AI mainly for object-oriented design practice.
- I asked AI to model a real-world Car as a Python class. The first draft covered basics (make, model, year, VIN), but it missed behavior. I revised my prompt to require fuel efficiency, tank/battery size, odometer, maintenance interval and methods like estimate_range(), trip_cost(), refuel/charge(), and service_due().
- I then asked for subclasses—GasCar, ElectricCar, Hybrid—and quick unit tests. Running the tests helped me spot edge cases (negative inputs, overfilling).
- I used AI to explain two errors I hit (AttributeError from a typo and a division by zero in estimate_range) and to generate docstrings I edited to match my code.
- I finished by writing my own version from scratch, using the AI output only as a reference.

What I learned: Good prompts ask for both attributes and behaviors plus tests. AI is a great starting point, but I still need to verify logic and performance myself.
